Assertions:
[DOM] After 'Continue' the step title is 'Check your email' and the address is masked {OBSERVED}
[STATE] No 405 / generic failure after Continue: POST /api/otp/request on the storefront origin answers 200 with succeeded=true {OBSERVED}
[STATE] The 6th digit auto-submits; the customer is signed in and leaves /sign-in (no returnUrl: lands on /) {OBSERVED}
[STATE] me.userName of the signed-in session identifies the account of {{USER_EMAIL}} {OBSERVED}
[NAV] After reload the session is still signed in {SPEC}

[DOM] Exactly one inline error alert is shown above the 'Code' field, text "That code didn't work." {OBSERVED}
[DOM] Under 'Code' there is no toast, no second alert and no raw translation key (e.g. shared.account.sign_in_form.errors...) {OBSERVED}
[STATE] The first cell of 'Code' is focused and the field accepts a new entry (it is not locked after the error) {OBSERVED}
[STATE] Still on /sign-in and not signed in after the wrong code {OBSERVED}
[STATE] Entering the real code afterwards signs the customer in {SPEC}

Preconditions:
[PRE:CLEAR_SESSION]
OtpSignIn.Enabled is on for {{STORE_ID}}
PasswordLogin:DetailedErrors is false on the target environment (platform appsettings, not changeable from a case). Probe: POST /api/otp/request for the unknown address; if error.code is user_not_found the environment shows detailed errors - mark BLOCKED, do not assert the masked screen against it

Assertions:
[DOM] The unknown address reaches the same 'Check your email' step as the known one, with a masked address and the same controls {SPEC}
[DOM] No "User not found" or other account-existence message is shown for the unknown address {OBSERVED}
[STATE] unknownScreen equals knownScreen in title, masking pattern and controls {SPEC}
[BODY] The journal holds no OtpSignInEmailNotification for the unknown address {OBSERVED}

[DOM] Under 'Email', the empty, no-domain and inner-space values each show a validation message and the page stays on the sign-in form with the 'Continue' button {OBSERVED}
[STATE] POST /api/otp/request is not sent for the empty, no-domain and inner-space values {OBSERVED}
[STATE] For the 255-char address either the client refuses it with a field message, or a request is sent and answers a 4xx validation error - never a 5xx and never a verify step; record which layer refused it {SPEC}
[STATE] The 254-char control address is not refused for LENGTH (the request is sent; any refusal is the unknown-email outcome) {SPEC}

[DOM] 'Code' holds exactly the six digits 123456 after the spaced paste and submits them (the alert "That code didn't work." follows) {OBSERVED}
[DOM] 'Code' drops the letter, holds 12456 and the 'Sign in' button stays disabled (nothing is submitted) {OBSERVED}
[STATE] The five-digit value stays in the cells and no POST /connect/token is sent {OBSERVED}
[DOM] 'Code' is cut to its first six digits 123456 and submitted once {SPEC}
[STATE] The real code afterwards signs the customer in {SPEC}

[DOM] After 'Resend code' the invalid-code error is gone, the code cells are empty and 'New code sent.' is announced {OBSERVED}
[DOM] After 'Use a different email' the email step is shown with no error from the previous attempt {OBSERVED}
[DOM] The 'Check your email' step for {{USER2_EMAIL}} shows that account's masked address, six empty code cells and no alert element {SPEC}
[STATE] No leftover alert from the first account survives either transition (single error list) {OBSERVED}

[DOM] /sign-in renders the 'Email' and 'Password' fields and a 'Sign in' button {OBSERVED}
[DOM] /sign-in has no 'Continue' button for a code, no six-cell code field and no link that switches to a one-time code {OBSERVED}
[STATE] error.code of POST /api/otp/request equals 'otp_disabled' {OBSERVED}
[STATE] Within the polling window the page does reflect the change (a setting that never propagates is the defect) {SPEC}

Preconditions:
[PRE:CLEAR_SESSION]
OtpSignIn.Enabled is on for {{STORE_ID}}
The homepage of {{STORE_ID}} carries a login section block (Page Builder login-form-section). B2B-store has none on vcptcore_qa1: if {{FRONT_URL}} shows no login section the case is BLOCKED, not FAIL

Assertions:
[DOM] After Continue the section title switches to 'Check your email' and shows the masked address {SPEC}
[STATE] The 6th digit auto-submits and the customer is signed in {SPEC}
[DOM] The section shows six code cells and the text 'Check your email', not the password form fields {SPEC}

[NAV] Back from a completed sign-in leaves /sign-in (there is no in-flow Back inside the code steps) {OBSERVED}
[STATE] Going back never shows a verify step that still holds the consumed code, and never re-submits it {SPEC}
[STATE] A second POST /connect/token is not sent by Back or Forward {SPEC}
[STATE] The session stays the signed-in customer; the page does not show an anonymous header after Back {SPEC}

[STATE] A reload on the verify step returns to the start (email) step with an empty Email field - the pending email is component state only {OBSERVED}
[DOM] The six cells of 'Code' are not shown after the reload, and no alert or spinner is shown {SPEC}
[STATE] A fresh request after the reload completes sign-in normally {SPEC}
[STATE] A reload after sign-in keeps the session {SPEC}

[STATE] Tab B shares the OTP-created session of tab A (same customer) {SPEC}
[NAV] After sign-out in tab B, tab A navigates to /account/orders and ends on /sign-in {SPEC}
[DOM] Tab A does not show the previous customer's orders or name {SPEC}
[STATE] No blank screen and no silent 401 loop in tab A {SPEC}

[DOM] The expired code shows the same single inline error as a wrong code, "That code didn't work.", with no blank screen {OBSERVED}
[STATE] The form stays usable: Resend and Use a different email still work {SPEC}
[STATE] A fresh code after the expiry signs the customer in {OBSERVED}

[DOM] After a 500, a malformed body and an aborted call the email step shows one error alert and the 'Continue' button is enabled again {SPEC}
[DOM] A blocked request (the missing-route case, 405) shows the generic 'Something went wrong' on the email step {OBSERVED}
[STATE] No infinite spinner for the 500, malformed-JSON and aborted cases (<=10s) {SPEC}
[STATE] A failed token call on the verify step leaves the form editable and retryable {SPEC}
[STATE] Once the interception is removed the normal journey completes {SPEC}

[STATE] An autofilled email is accepted by Continue: no "required" message and the request carries the autofilled value {SPEC}
[DOM] After the paste on the first cell, 'Code' holds all six digits of the code and the form submits {SPEC}
[STATE] The customer is signed in {SPEC}

[DOM] At 200% and 400% the six cells, 'Resend code' and 'Use a different email' are visible and clickable {SPEC}
[DOM] document.scrollWidth <= viewport width on the 'Check your email' step at 200% and at 400% {SPEC}
[DOM] At 400% the bounding boxes of the six cells and of 'Resend code' / 'Use a different email' do not intersect {SPEC}
[DOM] With reduced motion and dark mode the step stays readable and no control is hidden {SPEC}

[STATE] The step has no paged or filtered list (nothing to scroll or page) - the paging probe collapses to the request-loop check below {SPEC}
[STATE] Five rapid clicks do not produce an unbounded request chain: the number of /api/otp/request calls is bounded (one per accepted click) and the step ends in one consistent state {SPEC}
[DOM] The status shows one settled message, not a stack of "New code sent." lines {SPEC}

[DOM] With a 254/255-character address the text of 'Email' and its validation message stay inside the field box and document scrollWidth does not exceed the viewport width {SPEC}
[DOM] After each unbreakable paste 'Code' holds at most six digits and its six cells keep their single-row layout {SPEC}
[STATE] No horizontal page scroll appears at any point {SPEC}
[STATE] The real code afterwards signs the customer in {SPEC}
